# WSL: Docker Outside the Sandbox

When this environment is WSL (check `user_info` / `uname` for `microsoft-standard-WSL`), run **all Docker-related Shell commands with the sandbox disabled**.

## Why

Cursor’s default Shell sandbox hides `/var/run/docker.sock`. The Docker CLI then fails with “Cannot connect to the Docker daemon” even when `dockerd` is running in WSL.

## How

For any command that uses the Docker CLI or talks to the daemon (`docker`, `docker compose`, `docker-compose`, buildx, etc.), call the Shell tool with:

```text
required_permissions: ["all"]
```

Do this on the **first** attempt — do not first run sandboxed, see the socket error, then retry.

## Examples

- `docker build`, `docker run`, `docker images`, `docker ps`
- `docker compose up` / `docker compose build`
- Anything that needs `/var/run/docker.sock` or `/run/docker.sock`

## Not covered

Non-Docker commands can keep the default sandbox. Only disable it for Docker (or when another task truly needs host access).
